│ patch_description        │ Replace the random, unoptimized point sample with a deterministic differential-evolution  │
│                          │ search specialized for the Heilbronn objective. The search fixes three points at the      │
│                          │ vertices of a reference triangle and optimizes the remaining ten interior points. This    │
│                          │ guarantees a convex unit reference hull, makes every candidate feasible through           │
│                          │ reflection into the triangle, and permits direct maximization of the normalized minimum   │
│                          │ triangle area.                                                                            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ All 286 triangle determinants are evaluated simultaneously for a population of            │
│                          │ candidates. Selection uses the minimum determinant as the dominant term and a small bonus │
│                          │ for the lower tail of triangle areas, which avoids configurations where one triangle is   │
│                          │ improved at the expense of many nearly-degenerate ones. The fixed seed and fixed          │
│                          │ iteration schedule make the result reproducible.                                          │
