│ patch_name               │ bottleneck_coordinate_search                                                              │
│ patch_description        │ This replaces the purely random construction with a deterministic bottleneck-oriented     │
│                          │ coordinate search. Four points are fixed at the corners of the unit square, guaranteeing  │
│                          │ a convex hull of area one and making the normalized minimum triangle area equal to the    │
│                          │ raw minimum area. The remaining nine points are optimized through multiple seeded         │
│                          │ restarts.                                                                                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The search uses a smooth lower-tail objective: rather than optimizing only the single     │
│                          │ worst triangle, it emphasizes the collection of smallest triangle areas using a           │
│                          │ temperature-controlled soft minimum. This avoids unstable behavior where improving one    │
│                          │ degenerate triangle immediately creates another. Candidate moves are evaluated in batches │
│                          │ while only recomputing triangles incident to the moved point, making the optimization     │
│                          │ substantially more efficient than recalculating all geometry for every proposal.          │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
