│ patch_name               │ deterministic_triangle_annealing                                                          │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the random square sample with a deterministic multi-start simulated-annealing     │
│                          │ construction inside a fixed equilateral triangular hull. Fixing three hull vertices gives │
│                          │ a stable convex region, while all remaining points are represented by barycentric samples │
│                          │ and are therefore always inside that hull.                                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The optimization evaluates all 286 triangle areas simultaneously. Its annealing objective │
│                          │ is a smooth soft-minimum of normalized triangle areas, which gives useful progress even   │
│                          │ when the identity of the currently smallest triangle changes. Several deterministic       │
│                          │ restarts, decreasing perturbation radii, and a final exact-minimum selection              │
│                          │ substantially improve on an unstructured random configuration while retaining             │
│                          │ reproducibility and avoiding external dependencies.                                       │
