│ patch_name               │ deterministic_maximin13                                                                   │
│ patch_description        │ This version replaces the unstructured random sample with a deterministic maximin search. │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ It fixes four points at the corners of the unit square, guaranteeing a convex unit-area   │
│                          │ containing region, and optimizes the remaining nine interior points. The objective        │
│                          │ evaluates all 286 triangle determinants and uses a temperature-controlled soft-min        │
│                          │ objective so that optimization improves not only the single worst triangle but also the   │
│                          │ set of near-worst triangles. Several deterministic seeded restarts, annealed coordinate   │
│                          │ perturbations, and a final min-area polishing phase substantially improve the minimum     │
│                          │ normalized triangle area while retaining reproducibility and a compact dependency         │
│                          │ footprint.                                                                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The returned array remains a NumPy array of shape `(13, 2)` and all points remain inside  │
│                          │ the unit square.                                                                          │
