│ patch_name               │ adaptive_island_de                                                                        │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the basic `DE/rand/1` loop with a larger deterministic current-to-pbest           │
│                          │ differential-evolution search.  The smallest-area objective is highly nonsmooth: once a   │
│                          │ candidate has a few active limiting triangles, ordinary crossover frequently loses all    │
│                          │ useful structure.  Current-to-pbest mutation preserves good configurations while still    │
│                          │ using population differences for exploration.  Per-candidate mutation factors and         │
│                          │ crossover probabilities prevent the whole population from following one search scale.     │
│                          │ Periodic replacement of only the weakest candidates provides deterministic restart        │
│                          │ behavior without discarding the best geometric arrangements found so far.                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The additional evaluations are worthwhile because the former 72-member, 420-generation    │
│                          │ search explores only a small portion of the 20-dimensional barycentric parameter space.   │
│                          │ The return value remains reproducible because every operation uses the existing seeded    │
│                          │ generator.                                                                                │
