│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ consistent_annealing_score                                                                │
│ patch_description        │ The annealing loop changes the soft-min width at every iteration, but previously compared │
│                          │ a candidate evaluated at the new width against an incumbent score retained from the       │
│                          │ preceding width. This makes acceptance decisions inconsistent: narrowing the soft-min     │
│                          │ alone changes the objective even when the point set has not changed. Re-evaluating the    │
│                          │ incumbent at the current width produces a valid deterministic annealing comparison and    │
│                          │ lets late iterations genuinely optimize the near-minimum triangle constraints.            │
│ num_applied              │ 3                                                                                         │
