│ patch_name               │ critical_pair_refinement                                                                  │
│ patch_description        │ Add a deterministic joint two-point refinement stage before the existing one-point        │
│                          │ polishing phase. The strict coordinate search can become trapped when several active      │
│                          │ minimum-area triangles require two interior points to move cooperatively: every           │
│                          │ individual move temporarily worsens one bottleneck, even though a coupled displacement    │
│                          │ improves the true max-min objective. The added critical-pair moves select two movable     │
│                          │ vertices from the currently smallest triangle, test a small batch of correlated and       │
│                          │ independent joint perturbations, and accept only strict non-decreasing improvements. This │
│                          │ preserves determinism and feasibility in the unit square while providing an escape        │
│                          │ mechanism for coordinate-wise local optima.                                               │
