│ patch_name               │ critical_softmin_search                                                                   │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the raw minimum-only annealing objective with a stable soft-min objective over    │
│                          │ all 286 normalized triangle determinants. A raw minimum has large flat plateaus: moves    │
│                          │ that improve the second-, third-, or tenth-smallest triangle receive no signal. The       │
│                          │ soft-min preserves emphasis on bottleneck triangles while rewarding improvements to the   │
│                          │ near-critical set, which is especially useful for the highly nonsmooth Heilbronn          │
│                          │ objective.                                                                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The search also chooses movable vertices from the endpoints of currently critical         │
│                          │ triangles most iterations. This concentrates local refinement on the triangles limiting   │
│                          │ the configuration, while periodic unrestricted moves preserve the ability to reorganize   │
│                          │ the full point set. The best configuration is still selected strictly by the true minimum │
│                          │ triangle area, not the surrogate objective.                                               │
