│ patch_description        │ Add deterministic directed coordinate proposals derived from the area gradients of the    │
│                          │ currently smallest triangles incident to the point being updated. The existing search     │
│                          │ samples only random directions, despite already identifying the complete lower tail of    │
│                          │ the triangle-area spectrum. For a fixed point, each signed triangle determinant has a     │
│                          │ simple linear gradient; summing the ascent gradients of the tight incident constraints    │
│                          │ gives a local maximin-inspired direction that tends to expand several limiting triangles  │
│                          │ simultaneously.                                                                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Three of the random proposals are replaced by short, medium, and long moves along this    │
│                          │ lower-tail gradient. Random and broad exploration proposals remain available, while late  │
│                          │ coordinate polishing is unchanged. This should improve the probability that each sweep    │
│                          │ finds a genuine bottleneck-improving direction without increasing the number of triangle  │
│                          │ evaluations.                                                                              │
