│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ orbit_bundle13                                                                            │
│ patch_description        │ This implementation replaces the high-dimensional direct evolutionary search with a       │
│                          │ two-level constraint-bundle strategy. First, it searches a compact threefold-orbit        │
│                          │ family: one center point plus four rotated point orbits, with the outer orbit defining an │
│                          │ equilateral convex hull. This substantially reduces the difficult global-search dimension │
│                          │ while retaining asymmetric radial phases to avoid the collinearities caused by naïve      │
│                          │ rotational symmetry.                                                                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ A deterministic cross-entropy search identifies promising orbit parameters using a        │
│                          │ lexicographic bottleneck-and-lower-tail objective. It then expands the best symmetric     │
│                          │ candidate into unrestricted interior points and applies active-constraint local           │
│                          │ refinement: proposals preferentially move vertices belonging to currently small           │
│                          │ triangles, while only accepting improvements to the true minimum area or its lower-tail   │
│                          │ tie-breaker. The outer hull remains fixed and all movable points are projected into the   │
│                          │ enclosing triangle.                                                                       │
