│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ tailguided_square13                                                                       │
│ patch_description        │ This version keeps the unit-square hull, preserving exact normalized-area evaluation, but │
│                          │ replaces the single-proposal annealing loop with a batched tail-guided search. Each       │
│                          │ iteration generates multiple coordinated candidate moves around points involved in the    │
│                          │ currently smallest triangles, evaluates all candidates vectorially, and selects according │
│                          │ to a lexicographic low-tail objective: maximize the true minimum double-area first, then  │
│                          │ improve the mean of the smallest triangle areas.                                          │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The novel component is a deterministic active-constraint search: rather than smoothing    │
│                          │ every triangle equally, it repeatedly identifies the current bottleneck triangle graph,   │
│                          │ selects participating movable vertices, and tests a population of directional, isotropic, │
│                          │ and reflected proposals. This gives substantially more useful local exploration per       │
│                          │ determinant evaluation. A final strict polish retains only lexicographic improvements,    │
│                          │ directly incorporating the recommended low-tail selection strategy.                       │
