│ patch_name               │ coupled_bottleneck_moves                                                                  │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the unproductive long 16-start portfolio with the historically stronger 10 fully  │
│                          │ converged starts, then introduce deterministic coupled moves during the main search.      │
│                          │ Coordinate-only max-min ascent is commonly trapped when two interior points participate   │
│                          │ in competing tight triangles: neither point can move independently without reducing       │
│                          │ another active constraint. Periodic full-configuration pair proposals select vertices     │
│                          │ from the current lower area tail and test both correlated translations and independent    │
│                          │ displacements. Since acceptance uses the exact global minimum triangle area, these moves  │
│                          │ are monotone and cannot degrade a candidate. This directly targets the nonsmooth          │
│                          │ active-constraint geometry characteristic of Heilbronn configurations while keeping       │
│                          │ runtime near the proven 10-restart implementation rather than the current costly          │
│                          │ 16-restart version.                                                                       │
