│ patch_name               │ elite_constraint_exchange                                                                 │
│ patch_description        │ This redesign replaces the long single-trajectory coordinate walk with a deterministic    │
│                          │ population-based constraint-exchange search. It retains the unit-square hull anchors, so  │
│                          │ normalized minimum area equals raw minimum triangle area, but explores many qualitatively │
│                          │ different arrangements simultaneously.                                                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The main search uses a differential-evolution style population whose selection criterion  │
│                          │ transitions from a smooth lower-tail objective to strict max-min triangle area. This lets │
│                          │ early iterations escape lattice basins while late iterations optimize the actual          │
│                          │ evaluation metric. The best population members are then polished using dense              │
│                          │ deterministic coordinate rings with lexicographic lower-tail tie-breaking, preserving the │
│                          │ strict bottleneck while improving nearby active constraints.                              │
