│ patch_name               │ active_pair_repair                                                                        │
│ patch_description        │ Strengthen the coupled active-constraint repair phase. Near a max-min local optimum,      │
│                          │ improving a tight triangle often requires moving a pair of its vertices jointly;          │
│                          │ repeatedly selecting the first two vertices biases the existing repair toward one         │
│                          │ displacement mode. This edit cycles deterministically through every movable pair          │
│                          │ appearing in the current bottleneck triangle or lower-tail set, increases the number of   │
│                          │ repair attempts, and doubles the correlated/random candidate stencil. All candidates are  │
│                          │ still evaluated with the exact minimum-area objective and accepted only when              │
│                          │ non-decreasing, so this preserves deterministic feasibility while providing substantially │
│                          │ better escape from coordinate-wise traps.                                                 │
