│                          │ area changes linearly with displacement of one vertex in the direction perpendicular to   │
│                          │ the opposite edge. The existing isotropic random proposals only occasionally discover     │
│                          │ these productive directions. Replacing four of the twelve random directions by both       │
│                          │ normal orientations for each of the two tightest incident triangles preserves exploratory │
│                          │ diversity while systematically targeting the active max-min constraints. This is          │
