│ patch_description        │ This replaces repeated single-point random walks in a square with a population-based      │
│                          │ differential-evolution search inside a fixed triangular convex hull. The three hull       │
│                          │ vertices are fixed, all other points are projected into the triangle, and the hull area   │
│                          │ is constant, making normalization exact and stable. Differential evolution performs       │
│                          │ global recombination across whole configurations rather than becoming trapped in          │
│                          │ coordinate-wise lattice basins. A deterministic active-constraint coordinate polish then  │
│                          │ improves the exact smallest triangle area using dense directional candidates and          │
│                          │ lower-tail tie-breaking.                                                                  │
